<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Teacher Journey</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"></head><body><header><a class="brand" href="/">STEM Journey</a><nav><a href="/teacher">Teacher</a><a href="/student">Student</a><a href="/rubric">Rubric</a><a href="/student-evidence-template">Evidence Template</a></nav></header><main><section class="pagehead"><span class="pill">Teacher View</span><h1>Term Learning & Assessment Plan</h1><p>Use this page as the term overview. Open each week for the four-lesson sequence and expected evidence.</p></section><section class="weeklist"><% weeks.forEach(w=>{ %><article class="weekcard"><div class="weeknum">W<%= w.week %></div><div><h2><%= w.title %></h2><p><%= w.focus %></p><p><strong>Evidence focus:</strong> <%= w.lessons.map(l=>l.evidence).join(' • ') %></p><a href="/week/<%= w.week %>">Open week →</a></div></article><% }) %></section><section class="panel"><h2>Assessment model</h2><p>Assess individual process evidence as well as the team's final prototype. This prevents the result being determined only by whether the final mechanism works perfectly.</p><a class="button" href="/rubric">Open 100-mark rubric</a></section></main><footer>Year 9 STEM • Farting Bin Engineering Challenge • 7 weeks</footer><script src="/app.js"></script></body></html>